LazInk licensing
================

0BSD - the BSD Zero Clause License. Do whatever you want with this code.
You do not have to keep this notice, credit anyone, or ask. The full text
is in LICENSES/0BSD.txt.

That is the point of it, and it took some doing. Until 18 September 2026
LazInk drew with a renderer derived from Project JEDI's JVCL, which stayed
under MPL 1.1: the package carried two licenses, and anyone shipping a
program built with it owed recipients that renderer's source. That renderer
has been replaced by LazInk's own - inkrender.pas, inkbox.pas, inkdraw.pas -
and deleted, so there is no third-party code in the package and nothing left
to put conditions on it.

The credit does not depend on the license and is not going anywhere:
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md tells where LazInk came from - Tony Stone's forum
thread in 2021, wp's suggestion to take what was needed from JVCL and the
list box example he wrote, and the JVCL authors whose drawing code got it
off the ground. docs/RENDERER_CHANGES.md keeps the record of that renderer.
None of their code remains here; the thanks do.

Lazarus/LCL and Free Pascal are dependencies with their own licenses. They
are not relicensed by LazInk.
